msgid "Yes (deflation)"
msgstr "はい（デフレーション）"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:101
msgid "Explicitly separates predictive and orthogonal variation."
msgstr "予測変動と直交変動を明示的に分離します。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:102
msgid "DO"
msgstr "DO"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:105
msgid "Projects X onto the null space of y, then extracts components via PCA."
msgstr "X を y の零空間へ射影し、PCA によって成分を抽出します。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:107
msgid "A practical rule of thumb:"
msgstr "実用上の目安は次のとおりです。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:109
msgid ""
"Use **OSC (fearn)** as the default — it is non-iterative, deterministic, "
"and one component is often sufficient."
msgstr "デフォルトには **OSC (fearn)** を使用します。非反復的かつ決定論的で、多くの場合は1成分で十分です。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:111
msgid ""
"Use **OPLS** when you want an explicit separation of predictive and "
"orthogonal scores for further analysis."
msgstr "追加の分析に向けて予測スコアと直交スコアを明示的に分離する場合は **OPLS** を使用します。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:113
msgid "Use **DO** as a simple, fast baseline to compare against."
msgstr "単純で高速な比較用ベースラインとして **DO** を使用します。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:117
msgid ""
"Extracting too many orthogonal components risks **stripping predictive "
"variation** alongside the noise. Start with ``n_components=1`` and "
"increase only if cross-validation confirms improved model simplicity "
"without loss of prediction accuracy."
msgstr ""
"直交成分を抽出しすぎると、ノイズとともに **予測変動まで除去する** おそれがあります。"
"``n_components=1`` から始め、予測精度を損なわずにモデルが単純になることを交差検証で確認できた"
"場合にのみ増やしてください。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:123
msgid "Simulated dataset"
msgstr "シミュレーションデータセット"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:125
msgid ""
"The examples below use a simple synthetic dataset where the analyte "
"signal and the interference are known by construction — making it easy to"
" verify visually that each method removes the right variation."
msgstr ""
"以下の例では、検体シグナルと干渉が構成上既知である単純な合成データセットを使用します。"
"これにより、各手法が適切な変動を除去していることを視覚的に容易に確認できます。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:129
msgid ""
"The dataset consists of 50 spectra. Each spectrum is a mixture of an "
"analyte peak at channel 50 and an interference peak at channel 70. The "
"analyte amplitude scales linearly with the concentration ``y``, while the"
" interference amplitude is drawn from a uniform distribution that is "
"uncorrelated with ``y``."
msgstr ""
"データセットは50本のスペクトルで構成されます。各スペクトルは、チャンネル50の検体ピークと"
"チャンネル70の干渉ピークの混合です。検体の振幅は濃度 ``y`` に比例しますが、干渉の振幅は"
"``y`` と無相関な一様分布から生成されます。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:156
msgid ""
"50 synthetic spectra coloured by concentration. The analyte peak (channel"
" 50) tracks y; the interference peak (channel 70) is uncorrelated with y."
msgstr "濃度別に色分けした50本の合成スペクトル。検体ピーク（チャンネル50）は y に追従し、干渉ピーク（チャンネル70）は y と無相関です。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:166
msgid "Orthogonal Signal Correction (OSC)"
msgstr "直交信号補正（OSC）"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:168
msgid ""
"Introduced by Wold et al. (1998) [2]_, OSC iteratively finds components "
"in ``X`` that have maximum variance *and* are orthogonal to ``y``, then "
"removes them by deflation. It belongs to **Group 1** of Svensson et al. "
"[1]_: a single component can substantially reduce the complexity of a "
"downstream PLS model."
msgstr ""
"Wold ら（1998）[2]_ が提案した OSC は、``X`` 内で分散が最大であり、かつ ``y`` に直交する"
"成分を反復的に求め、デフレーションによって除去します。これは Svensson ら [1]_ の **グループ1** "
"に属し、1つの成分で後段の PLS モデルの複雑さを大幅に減らせます。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:173
msgid "Three algorithmic variants are available via the ``method`` parameter:"
msgstr "``method`` パラメーターでは、3種類のアルゴリズムを選択できます。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:179
msgid "``method``"
msgstr "``method``"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:180
msgid "Algorithm"
msgstr "アルゴリズム"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:182
msgid "``\"wold\"``"
msgstr "``\"wold\"``"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:183
msgid ""
"Iterative NIPALS-style. Alternates between score estimation and "
"orthogonality constraint until convergence."
msgstr "反復型の NIPALS 形式。収束するまでスコア推定と直交性制約を交互に適用します。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:185
msgid "Original formulation [2]_. Can be slow for large datasets."
msgstr "原始的な定式化 [2]_。大規模データセットでは低速になる場合があります。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:186
msgid "``\"sjoblom\"``"
msgstr "``\"sjoblom\"``"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:187
msgid ""
"Modified iteration using the pseudo-inverse of ``y`` to enforce "
"orthogonality directly."
msgstr "``y`` の擬似逆行列を使用して直交性を直接課す修正反復法。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:189
msgid "Often converges faster than ``\"wold\"`` [3]_."
msgstr "多くの場合 ``\"wold\"`` より速く収束します [3]_。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:190
msgid "``\"fearn\"``"
msgstr "``\"fearn\"``"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:191
msgid ""
"Direct (non-iterative). Projects ``X`` onto the null space of ``y`` and "
"extracts dominant components via SVD."
msgstr "直接法（非反復）。``X`` を ``y`` の零空間へ射影し、SVD によって支配的な成分を抽出します。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:193
msgid "No convergence issues; fast and deterministic [4]_."
msgstr "収束の問題がなく、高速かつ決定論的です [4]_。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:209
msgid ""
"OSC-corrected spectra. The interference peak at channel 70 is suppressed;"
" the analyte peak at channel 50 remains scaled by concentration."
msgstr "OSC 補正済みスペクトル。チャンネル70の干渉ピークは抑制され、チャンネル50の検体ピークは濃度に応じた大きさを維持しています。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:219
msgid "Orthogonal PLS (OPLS)"
msgstr "直交 PLS（OPLS）"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:221
msgid ""
"Introduced by Trygg & Wold (2002) [5]_, OPLS extends PLS regression by "
"explicitly separating the predictive and orthogonal components of ``X``. "
"It belongs to **Group 2** of Svensson et al. [1]_: each component removed"
" corresponds to exactly one fewer PLS component in the downstream model."
msgstr ""
"Trygg と Wold（2002）[5]_ が提案した OPLS は、``X`` の予測成分と直交成分を明示的に分離することで"
"PLS 回帰を拡張します。これは Svensson ら [1]_ の **グループ2** に属し、除去する成分1つにつき、"
"後段モデルで必要な PLS 成分がちょうど1つ減ります。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:240
msgid ""
"OPLS-corrected spectra. The interference peak at channel 70 is "
"suppressed; the analyte peak at channel 50 remains scaled by "
"concentration."
msgstr "OPLS 補正済みスペクトル。チャンネル70の干渉ピークは抑制され、チャンネル50の検体ピークは濃度に応じた大きさを維持しています。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:250
msgid "Direct Orthogonalization (DO)"
msgstr "直接直交化（DO）"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:252
msgid ""
"Introduced by Andersson (1999) [6]_, DO is a non-iterative method. It "
"projects ``X`` onto the null space of ``y`` to isolate the variation "
"orthogonal to ``y``, then extracts the dominant directions of that "
"residual via PCA and subtracts them from the original ``X``. Like OPLS it"
" belongs to **Group 2** of Svensson et al. [1]_: one component removed "
"equals one fewer PLS component downstream. It is computationally the "
"lightest of the three and is useful as a fast, transparent baseline."
msgstr ""
"Andersson（1999）[6]_ が提案した DO は非反復法です。``X`` を ``y`` の零空間へ射影して ``y`` に"
"直交する変動を分離し、その残差の支配的な方向を PCA で抽出して元の ``X`` から差し引きます。"
"OPLS と同様に Svensson ら [1]_ の **グループ2** に属し、1成分の除去は後段の PLS 成分1つの削減に"
"対応します。3手法の中で計算負荷が最も小さく、高速で明快なベースラインとして有用です。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:274
msgid ""
"DO-corrected spectra. The interference peak at channel 70 is suppressed; "
"the analyte peak at channel 50 remains scaled by concentration."
msgstr "DO 補正済みスペクトル。チャンネル70の干渉ピークは抑制され、チャンネル50の検体ピークは濃度に応じた大きさを維持しています。"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:282
msgid "Fitting in a Pipeline"
msgstr "Pipeline での適合"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:284
msgid ""
"All three transformers follow the standard sklearn API and compose freely"
" with other steps:"
msgstr "3つのトランスフォーマーはいずれも標準の sklearn API に従い、他のステップと自由に組み合わせられます。"

